[{:db/id 17592186133821 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-a03feca5-d649-5b96-991d-3e2972b12233"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-a03feca5-d649-5b96-991d-3e2972b12233" :question/id #uuid "a03feca5-d649-5b96-991d-3e2972b12233" :question/math-academy-id "q-95937" :question/problem "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} & {r}_{13} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22} & {r}_{23} \\\\ 0 & 0 & {r}_{33}\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. You're given that the system of equations given below connects the columns of $Q$ and the columns of $A.$  \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{2}+{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{3}-{q}_{1}+2{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWhat is the value of ${r}_{11}+{r}_{12}+{r}_{33}?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's rewrite the vectors ${a}_{1},{a}_{2},{a}_{3}$ as a linear combination of the vectors ${q}_{1},{q}_{2},{q}_{3}:$\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1}=\\frac{1}{3}{a}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{2}=\\frac{1}{2}{a}_{2}+{q}_{1} \\\\ {q}_{3}=\\frac{1}{4}{a}_{3}-{q}_{1}+2{q}_{2}\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,{\\begin{aligned}{a}_{1}=3{q}_{1} \\\\ {a}_{2}=-2{q}_{1}+2{q}_{2} \\\\ {a}_{3}=4{q}_{1}-8{q}_{2}+4{q}_{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, this system can be written in matrix form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {a}_{1} & {a}_{2} & {a}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}| & | & | \\\\ {q}_{1} & {q}_{2} & {q}_{3} \\\\ | & | & |\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}3 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n{r}_{11}+{r}_{12}+{r}_{33}=3+(-2)+4=5.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-84577b17-c582-5baa-9501-36a73798f439"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-84577b17-c582-5baa-9501-36a73798f439" :answer-field/id #uuid "84577b17-c582-5baa-9501-36a73798f439" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-cbb4da72-b7ae-5fa0-aa7f-27b95ecda700" :answer-field/choices ["answer-2c232a99-6645-5177-89dc-66f13905956a" "answer-ad2e1681-8914-5558-96cf-ff55332d7ba4" "answer-cbb4da72-b7ae-5fa0-aa7f-27b95ecda700" "answer-bdaadcc3-b0d6-5daa-b301-47336aa1a8b4" "answer-713fedd8-bf09-5849-a1cc-c36eb8963d22"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2c232a99-6645-5177-89dc-66f13905956a" :answer/id #uuid "2c232a99-6645-5177-89dc-66f13905956a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ad2e1681-8914-5558-96cf-ff55332d7ba4" :answer/id #uuid "ad2e1681-8914-5558-96cf-ff55332d7ba4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-cbb4da72-b7ae-5fa0-aa7f-27b95ecda700" :answer/id #uuid "cbb4da72-b7ae-5fa0-aa7f-27b95ecda700" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-bdaadcc3-b0d6-5daa-b301-47336aa1a8b4" :answer/id #uuid "bdaadcc3-b0d6-5daa-b301-47336aa1a8b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-713fedd8-bf09-5849-a1cc-c36eb8963d22" :answer/id #uuid "713fedd8-bf09-5849-a1cc-c36eb8963d22" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186133863 :knowledge-point/questions ["question-3591a132-7ac4-53c0-88c4-ee928e48a3a0" "question-8b80e943-ecec-54be-8ddd-ec70be544570"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "question-3591a132-7ac4-53c0-88c4-ee928e48a3a0" :question/id #uuid "3591a132-7ac4-53c0-88c4-ee928e48a3a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-95943" :question/problem "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{q}_{11} & {q}_{12} \\\\ {q}_{21} & {q}_{22} \\\\ {q}_{31} & {q}_{32}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. Given that the columns ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ of $A$ are orthogonal, and that the columns ${q}_{1},{q}_{2}$ of $Q$ were obtained by normalizing the columns of $A,$ what is the value of ${q}_{31}\\cdot {r}_{11}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the columns of $A$ are already orthogonal, to construct an orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we simply normalize ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{‖{a}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{‖{a}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, pre-multiplying both sides of $A=QR$ by ${Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{6} & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{31}\\cdot {r}_{11}=-\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{6}}\\cdot \\sqrt{6}=-2.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-9c762c76-71d9-5aca-b185-d376fcab2ad5"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-9c762c76-71d9-5aca-b185-d376fcab2ad5" :answer-field/id #uuid "9c762c76-71d9-5aca-b185-d376fcab2ad5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-25368ac6-b32f-5b26-8c46-331ac1522f54" :answer-field/choices ["answer-e6e0f3fd-8867-5cbf-95df-3e0275090b4f" "answer-25368ac6-b32f-5b26-8c46-331ac1522f54" "answer-aff7607c-ce12-5a45-9cb9-bbc45508055e" "answer-ddbdf48a-0960-5123-be14-52d24536ef82" "answer-a0313793-4999-5aed-ac02-21acda57bbd4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e6e0f3fd-8867-5cbf-95df-3e0275090b4f" :answer/id #uuid "e6e0f3fd-8867-5cbf-95df-3e0275090b4f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-25368ac6-b32f-5b26-8c46-331ac1522f54" :answer/id #uuid "25368ac6-b32f-5b26-8c46-331ac1522f54" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-aff7607c-ce12-5a45-9cb9-bbc45508055e" :answer/id #uuid "aff7607c-ce12-5a45-9cb9-bbc45508055e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{6}}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-ddbdf48a-0960-5123-be14-52d24536ef82" :answer/id #uuid "ddbdf48a-0960-5123-be14-52d24536ef82" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a0313793-4999-5aed-ac02-21acda57bbd4" :answer/id #uuid "a0313793-4999-5aed-ac02-21acda57bbd4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\sqrt{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-8b80e943-ecec-54be-8ddd-ec70be544570" :question/id #uuid "8b80e943-ecec-54be-8ddd-ec70be544570" :question/math-academy-id "q-96027" :question/problem "$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{q}_{11} & {q}_{12} \\\\ {q}_{21} & {q}_{22} \\\\ {q}_{31} & {q}_{32}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}{r}_{11} & {r}_{12} \\\\ 0 & {r}_{22}\\end{aligned}]}}.\n$$\n\nConsider the QR factorization of the matrix $A$ shown above. Given that the columns ${a}_{1},{a}_{2}$ of $A$ are orthogonal, and that the columns ${q}_{1},{q}_{2}$ of $Q$ were obtained by normalizing the columns of $A,$ what is the value of ${q}_{22}\\cdot {r}_{22}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since the columns of $A$ are already orthogonal, to construct an orthogonal matrix $Q,$ we simply normalize ${a}_{1}$ and ${a}_{2}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{q}_{1} & =\\frac{{a}_{1}}{‖{a}_{1}‖}=\\frac{1}{9}[\\begin{aligned}7 \\\\ 4 \\\\ 4\\end{aligned}] \\\\ {q}_{2} & =\\frac{{a}_{2}}{‖{a}_{2}‖}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, pre-multiplying both sides of $A=QR$ by ${Q}^{T},$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}R & ={Q}^{T}\\,A \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{9} & \\frac{4}{9} & \\frac{4}{9} \\\\ 0 & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have the following QR factorization of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\overset{A}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}7 & 0 \\\\ 4 & 1 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]}}=\\overset{Q}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{7}{9} & 0 \\\\ \\frac{4}{9} & \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\\\ \\frac{4}{9} & -\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\end{aligned}]}}\\overset{R}{\\overset{⏞}{[\\begin{aligned}9 & 0 \\\\ 0 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}]}}\n$$\n\nFinally, ${q}_{22}\\cdot {r}_{22}=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=1.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-84ec1a22-6484-5de6-851b-ba1cc03d10d3"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-84ec1a22-6484-5de6-851b-ba1cc03d10d3" :answer-field/id #uuid "84ec1a22-6484-5de6